# What this package may never name, anywhere under lib/ and test/.
#
# THE TEST FOR A WORD: could a vendor with the same tools and a completely different product still
# use this package with that word in it? This package's tools are the declaration grammar it
# defines itself, the chart and its repository index, the container build file, the tag lists of
# registries speaking the distribution protocol, and the public release feeds — so it may say
# chart, dependency, index, tag, registry, release and store, because those are the tools' own
# words. A name of one product measured with them fails and goes on this list.
#
# One word per line. Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored; everything else is matched
# case-insensitively and word-anchored, so a longer name that merely contains a word is no
# occurrence of it.
#
# WORD-ANCHORED CUTS BOTH WAYS, and the blocks below are written knowing it. Anything that is not a
# letter or a digit ends a word, so a bare name reports every longer one built on it with a
# separator — and a longer name built WITHOUT a separator is a different word: `git` on this list
# does not report `github`, which is one of this package's release feeds and stays sayable.
#
# THE LIST LIVES HERE, UNDER tool/, AND NOT BESIDE THE CHECK THAT READS IT. The scan reads test/ to
# the byte, so a list written into test/checks/tool_purity_test.dart would itself be an occurrence
# of every word on it and the check could never pass.

# The product this package serves first, the platform it stands on, and the organisation behind
# both. This block stands on every list in this tree, word for word.
hostyour
digita
digitacloud
digitaplatform
simetrix
simetrixch

# That product's choices: the distribution it installs, the components it deploys, the tools it
# drives those components with, the vendors it rents from, and the authority it gets its
# certificates from. Each is a fact of one product, not of a pin or of the feeds pins are checked
# against. `helm` is absent because the chart and its repository index ARE this package's tools,
# and `snap` because the snap store is one of its feeds; every component NAME that happens to be
# deployed somewhere — including those two tools' products — is still a fact of a declaration
# file, never of this package.
microk8s
argocd
tekton
zot
authentik
external-secrets
vault
kubectl
git
netplan
cloudflare
hetzner
letsencrypt

# That product's own domain words.
tenant
consumer
trunk
